# Taskmark file conventions

When creating or editing files under `taskmark/`:

- Keep required YAML frontmatter including `size`, `points`, `estimate_minutes`, `actual_minutes`, `session_cap_minutes`, sources/basis fields, and standard id/status/parent fields.
- Do **not** hand-set `status` except via `blocked` / `cancelled`; after edits run sync-status.
- **Never** set `actual_minutes` from calendar span (`completed_at − started_at`). Use billable work-log sessions only (idle auto-cap: next-day 12:00 UTC; session_cap_minutes default 480).
- Idle: auto-close open sessions at next-day 12:00 UTC when syncing / starting / completing work.
- **Work log** and **Commits** on every item; **Prompt & feedback** on stories/tasks/bugs.
- Refresh `INDEX.md` (Points / Est / Actual) and `VELOCITY.md` on sync.
- Follow `taskmark-conventions` skill templates.
